[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glfw/glfw/issues/comments/1048332889","html_url":"https://github.com/glfw/glfw/issues/1395#issuecomment-1048332889","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glfw/glfw/issues/1395","id":1048332889,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAJFXBc4-fEpZ","user":{"login":"jjYBdx4IL","id":491220,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTIyMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/491220?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL","html_url":"https://github.com/jjYBdx4IL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-23T00:14:34Z","updated_at":"2022-02-23T00:29:36Z","body":"It would be nice to have GLFW as a thin cross-platform window handling layer for DLL plugins/modules.\r\n\r\nBTW: the problem isn't the window class name per se (unique per HINSTANCE). It's rather that GLFW gets the HINSTANCE for the main process into which it gets loaded into. Instead, it should use the module handle:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndiff --git a/include/GLFW/glfw3native.h b/include/GLFW/glfw3native.h\r\nindex e680c1e3..9154c711 100644\r\n--- a/include/GLFW/glfw3native.h\r\n+++ b/include/GLFW/glfw3native.h\r\n@@ -169,6 +169,13 @@ GLFWAPI const char* glfwGetWin32Monitor(GLFWmonitor* monitor);\r\n  *  @ingroup native\r\n  */\r\n GLFWAPI HWND glfwGetWin32Window(GLFWwindow* window);\r\n+\r\n+// Plugins need to set this before using any parts of GLFW to avoid clashes\r\n+// with other plugins potentially also using GLFW (also, DLLs shouldn't\r\n+// register window classes using the EXE's instance handle). This should\r\n+// be more in accordance with Win32 rules than the redefinition of\r\n+// _GLFW_WNDCLASSNAME. It's also more flexible.\r\n+GLFWAPI void glfwSetHinstance(void* hInst);\r\n #endif\r\n\r\n #if defined(GLFW_EXPOSE_NATIVE_WGL)\r\ndiff --git a/src/init.c b/src/init.c\r\nindex a7b5af63..0d1532c1 100644\r\n--- a/src/init.c\r\n+++ b/src/init.c\r\n@@ -41,6 +41,10 @@\r\n //\r\n // Any other global variable is a bug\r\n\r\n+#if defined(_GLFW_WIN32)\r\n+void* hInstance = NULL;\r\n+#endif\r\n+\r\n // Global state shared between compilation units of GLFW\r\n //\r\n _GLFWlibrary _glfw = { GLFW_FALSE };\r\ndiff --git a/src/internal.h b/src/internal.h\r\nindex f87c2f93..5264d59d 100644\r\n--- a/src/internal.h\r\n+++ b/src/internal.h\r\n@@ -518,6 +518,10 @@ struct _GLFWmutex\r\n     _GLFW_PLATFORM_MUTEX_STATE;\r\n };\r\n\r\n+#if defined(_GLFW_WIN32)\r\n+void* __hInstance;\r\n+#endif\r\n+\r\n // Library global data\r\n //\r\n struct _GLFWlibrary\r\ndiff --git a/src/win32_init.c b/src/win32_init.c\r\nindex 970da06e..e292bc9e 100644\r\n--- a/src/win32_init.c\r\n+++ b/src/win32_init.c\r\n@@ -68,6 +68,13 @@ BOOL WINAPI DllMain(HINSTANCE instance, DWORD reason, LPVOID reserved)\r\n\r\n #endif // _GLFW_BUILD_DLL\r\n\r\n+#if defined(_GLFW_WIN32)\r\n+void glfwSetHinstance(void* hInst)\r\n+{\r\n+    __hInstance = hInst;\r\n+}\r\n+#endif\r\n+\r\n // Load necessary libraries (DLLs)\r\n //\r\n static GLFWbool loadLibraries(void)\r\n@@ -348,7 +355,7 @@ static GLFWbool createHelperWindow(void)\r\n                         WS_CLIPSIBLINGS | WS_CLIPCHILDREN,\r\n                         0, 0, 1, 1,\r\n                         NULL, NULL,\r\n-                        GetModuleHandleW(NULL),\r\n+                        __hInstance != NULL ? __hInstance : GetModuleHandleW(NULL),\r\n                         NULL);\r\n\r\n     if (!_glfw.win32.helperWindowHandle)\r\ndiff --git a/src/win32_joystick.c b/src/win32_joystick.c\r\nindex 9c71d114..12068d89 100644\r\n--- a/src/win32_joystick.c\r\n+++ b/src/win32_joystick.c\r\n@@ -574,7 +574,7 @@ GLFWbool _glfwPlatformInitJoysticks(void)\r\n {\r\n     if (_glfw.win32.dinput8.instance)\r\n     {\r\n-        if (FAILED(DirectInput8Create(GetModuleHandle(NULL),\r\n+        if (FAILED(DirectInput8Create(__hInstance != NULL ? __hInstance : GetModuleHandleW(NULL),\r\n                                       DIRECTINPUT_VERSION,\r\n                                       &IID_IDirectInput8W,\r\n                                       (void**) &_glfw.win32.dinput8.api,\r\ndiff --git a/src/win32_window.c b/src/win32_window.c\r\nindex 52a9c680..3ece4503 100644\r\n--- a/src/win32_window.c\r\n+++ b/src/win32_window.c\r\n@@ -1266,7 +1266,7 @@ static int createNativeWindow(_GLFWwindow* window,\r\n                                            fullWidth, fullHeight,\r\n                                            NULL, // No parent window\r\n                                            NULL, // No window menu\r\n-                                           GetModuleHandleW(NULL),\r\n+                                            __hInstance != NULL ? __hInstance : GetModuleHandleW(NULL),\r\n                                            (LPVOID) wndconfig);\r\n\r\n     free(wideTitle);\r\n@@ -1355,12 +1355,12 @@ GLFWbool _glfwRegisterWindowClassWin32(void)\r\n     wc.cbSize        = sizeof(wc);\r\n     wc.style         = CS_HREDRAW | CS_VREDRAW | CS_OWNDC;\r\n     wc.lpfnWndProc   = (WNDPROC) windowProc;\r\n-    wc.hInstance     = GetModuleHandleW(NULL);\r\n+    wc.hInstance     = __hInstance != NULL ? __hInstance : GetModuleHandleW(NULL);\r\n     wc.hCursor       = LoadCursorW(NULL, IDC_ARROW);\r\n     wc.lpszClassName = _GLFW_WNDCLASSNAME;\r\n\r\n     // Load user-provided icon if available\r\n-    wc.hIcon = LoadImageW(GetModuleHandleW(NULL),\r\n+    wc.hIcon = LoadImageW(__hInstance != NULL ? __hInstance : GetModuleHandleW(NULL),\r\n                           L\"GLFW_ICON\", IMAGE_ICON,\r\n                           0, 0, LR_DEFAULTSIZE | LR_SHARED);\r\n     if (!wc.hIcon)\r\n@@ -1385,7 +1385,7 @@ GLFWbool _glfwRegisterWindowClassWin32(void)\r\n //\r\n void _glfwUnregisterWindowClassWin32(void)\r\n {\r\n-    UnregisterClassW(_GLFW_WNDCLASSNAME, GetModuleHandleW(NULL));\r\n+    UnregisterClassW(_GLFW_WNDCLASSNAME, __hInstance != NULL ? __hInstance : GetModuleHandleW(NULL));\r\n }\r\n\r\n\r\n@@ -2377,7 +2377,7 @@ VkResult _glfwPlatformCreateWindowSurface(VkInstance instance,\r\n\r\n     memset(&sci, 0, sizeof(sci));\r\n     sci.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_WIN32_SURFACE_CREATE_INFO_KHR;\r\n-    sci.hinstance = GetModuleHandle(NULL);\r\n+    sci.hinstance = __hInstance != NULL ? __hInstance : GetModuleHandleW(NULL);\r\n     sci.hwnd = window->win32.handle;\r\n\r\n     err = vkCreateWin32SurfaceKHR(instance, &sci, allocator, surface);\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nYou could rename this issue to \"add module encapsulation support\". For that purpose, I also wonder if there are any other such \"transgressions\" hidden in the GLFW code. Anything that prevents module unload?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glfw/glfw/issues/comments/1048332889/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jjYBdx4IL","id":491220,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTIyMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/491220?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL","html_url":"https://github.com/jjYBdx4IL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjYBdx4IL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https: